==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fr|strident}}, from {{der|en|la|strīdēns}}, present active participle of {{m|la|strīdō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|/ˈstɹaɪ.dənt/|[ˈstɹaɪdˀnt]|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-strident.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[loud|Loud]]; [[shrill]], [[piercing]], high-[[pitch]]ed; [[rough]]-sounding
#: {{ux|en|The trumpet sounded '''strident''' against the string orchestra.}}
# [[grating|Grating]] or [[obnoxious]]
#: {{ux|en|The artist chose a '''strident''' mixture of colors.}}
# {{lb|en|nonstandard}} [[vigorous|Vigorous]]; making [[stride]]s
#* {{quote-journal|2003|November 6|Stuart Cosgrove|Taylor slagging Saddam shame.|Daily Record|city=Glasgow|url=http://www.highbeam.com/doc/1G1-109818227.html
|passage=Under David Taylor's stewardship, the SFA has made '''strident''' progress.}}

